mean"],["The mean of 7 numbers is 9. When one more number, 17, is added, the new mean is:",["11.43","13","9","10"],"D",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The mean of 5 numbers is 27. When one more number, 51, is added, the new mean is:",["37.2","39","31","27"],"C",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The mean of 5 numbers is 18. When one more number, 42, is added, the new mean is:",["30","26.4","22","18"],"C",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The mean of 7 numbers is 24. When one more number, 40, is added, the new mean is:",["26","24","29.71","32"],"A",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The mean of 6 numbers is 30. When one more number, 44, is added, the new mean is:",["30","37","37.33","32"],"D",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The mean of 5 numbers is 9. When one more number, 33, is added, the new mean is:",["13","21","15.6","9"],"A",5,0,"gen-maths-m11-new-mean"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 100–110 is:",["105","110","100","10"],"A",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 40–50 is:",["45","10","50","40"],"A",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 20–25 is:",["25","5","22.5","20"],"C",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 70–80 is:",["70","10","75","80"],"C",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 30–40 is:",["30","35","10","40"],"B",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"],["The class mark (mid-point) of the class 140–160 is:",["150","20","140","160"],"A",1,0,"gen-maths-m11-class-mark"]]$j$::jsonb, true);
select public.prepify_load_bank('Physics', 1, $j$[["If you are in chemistry lab which device help to calculate mass",["Stop watch","Calculator","Physical balance","Vernier caliper"],"C",5,1,"2a70d361ff7e"],["The SI unit of luminous intensity is",["Newton","Kelvin","Kilogram","Candela"],"D",5,1,"b5e8205d0e0e"],["What is the name of unit written as MW",["Milli watt","Mega watt","Million watt","Kilowatt"],"B",5,1,"3eebba22b906"],["The upper jaws of vernier caliper is used to calculate",["Volume","Internal diameter","External diameter","Area"],"B",5,1,"cdb26f72bcb3"],["The most precise device in vernier caliper and screw Gauge is",["Screw Gauge","Vernier caliper","Both","None"],"A",5,1,"809a51256de5"],["The doubts present in our measurements is known as",["Precision","Accuracy","Errors","Significant digits"],"C",5,1,"3628a0d0c56d"],["The least count for digital stop watch is",["1s","0.1s","0.01s","0.001s"],"C",5,1,"e89a99c7ba52"],["Measuring cylinder is used to calculate",["Length","Volume","Area","Mass"],"B",5,1,"d8a1c70ea8a7"],["If the car is crashed in west with 30m/s the quantity is",["Scalar","Base","Non physical","Vector"],"D",5,1,"9f48ed2f145a"],["Which type of quantity momentum is",["Vector","Scalar","Base","Non physical"],"A",5,1,"5af6be11cb19"],["Quantity that represent with letter and arrow head over it is",["Base","Derived","Scalar","Vector"],"D",5,1,"c7a5b11664a6"],["The rule used to calculate the sum of vectors is",["Subtraction","Graphical analysis","Head to tail rule","Cramer's rule"],"C",5,1,"9d94488ee64c"],["The frame of reference that describe the position of point or object",["Origin system","Coordinate system","SI system","None of these"],"B",5,1,"75be44190557"],["A meter ruler has 100 cm divisions.Each centimeter is further subdivided into",["1 millimeters","10 millimeters","50 millimeters","100 millimeters"],"B",5,1,"2cf2f5fb27c6"],["You have a page and beaker which device is used to calculate thickness",["Vernier caliper","Screw Gauge","Meter ruler","Measuring tape"],"B",5,1,"f33b3822a97e"],["The prefix tera is equal to",["10¹²","10¹⁰","10¹⁵","10¹⁶"],"A",5,1,"53a2262672b4"],["We use measuring cylinder to calculate volume. Which method is used in it?",["Head to tail","Displacement","Scalar","Significant digits"],"B",5,1,"5b924310cfb3"],["Measured and exact values are the types of",["Measurements","Scalar","Errors","Vectors"],"A",5,1,"a6d3e760a028"],["Which type of error is removed by calibration of an instrument",["Random","Systematic","Personal","External"],"B",5,1,"63612ba6011a"],["For scientific notation international accepted practice is that their should be how many digits before the decimal point",["Two","Three","Four","One"],"D",5,1,"3447578fffe4"],["The term used internationally for multiples and submultiples of various units are known as",["Standard","Scientific notation","Prefixes","All of above"],"C",5,1,"50e62f2afb5c"],["Separation between division on the vernier scale of vernier caliper is",["1cm","1mm","0.9mm","All of them"],"C",5,1,"2a0fdc298ab3"],["Which type of error is often described as 'bias'",["Random","Systematic","Measurement","Human"],"B",5,1,"486a5f83d379"],["Which quantity is largest?",["5 mm","5000 μm","0.005 m","All are equal"],"D",3,0,"c3e18b647b2e"],["Which reading has four significant figures?",["0.0205","2.05","205","20.50"],"D",3,0,"bca1a6548740"],["This means it can measure:",["Only whole millimetres","Up to 0.1 mm","Up to 0.01 mm","Up to 1 mm"],"C",3,0,"7e3593634563"],["The volume of the stone is:",["15 cm³","40 cm³","55 cm³","95 cm³"],"A",3,0,"b167de7020d3"],["To reduce random error, he should:",["Measure one oscillation only.","Measure many oscillations and find the average.","Use a larger pendulum.","Use a ruler."],"B",3,0,"694a91744839"],["A scale always shows 0.2 kg more than the true value. This is an example of:",["Random error","Systematic error","Human error","Percentage error"],"B",3,0,"65e5d63bbf7c"],["How many base SI units are there?",["5","6","7","8"],"C",3,0,"85507b0ba132"],["Round off 5.886 to two decimal places.",["5.87","5.89","5.80","5.90"],"B",3,0,"36a561420846"],["A screw gauge is more precise than a vernier caliper because it has:",["greater size","more scales","smaller least count","longer spindle"],"C",3,0,"a0770e87795a"],["A reading is written as 8.05 cm. Which digit is uncertain according to the idea of significant figures?",["8","5","0","All digits equally"],"B",3,0,"e6c623a91033"],["Which instrument is most suitable for measuring the internal diameter of a hollow tube?",["Measuring tape","Meter rule","Vernier caliper","Stopwatch"],"C",3,0,"ed2a7f170076"],["Which pair contains one scalar and one vector quantity?",["Speed and velocity","Force and weight","Distance and time","Mass and energy"],"A",3,0,"e4473686cd25"],["The number 3.45 × 10⁷ contains:",["7 significant figures","3 significant figures","2 significant figures","45 significant figures"],"B",3,0,"f86564e3a80f"],["Its diameter in millimeters is:",["0.2 mm","2 mm","20 mm","200 mm"],"B",3,0,"212356466f6e"],["The value 5 × 10⁶ m can be written as:",["5 km","5 Mm","5 μm","5 nm"],"B",3,0,"b6080be9e37b"],["The number 0.00072 is written in scientific notation as:",["7.2 × 10⁻⁵","7.2 × 10⁻⁴","72 × 10⁻⁵","0.72 × 10⁻³"],"B",3,0,"7213464ab3b6"],["A student writes 56000 = 5.6 × 10⁻⁴. What is wrong?",["The coefficient is wrong.","The power of 10 should be positive.","Scientific notation cannot be used.","Nothing is wrong."],"B",3,1,"e35a41bab742"],["Which of the following is a physical quantity?",["Honesty","Happiness","Intelligence","Length"],"D",3,0,"5a03e9031f5c"],["A measurement without a unit is:",["Complete","Incomplete","Accurate","Precise"],"B",3,0,"e0d6ffd19939"],["This quantity is most likely:",["Base quantity","Derived quantity","Non-physical quantity","Fundamental quantity"],"B",3,0,"607d1dde7e6f"],["Which part of the measurement changes when the same length is expressed in cm instead of m?",["Unit only","Numerical magnitude only","Both magnitude and unit","Neither"],"C",3,0,"2f6802e6fbdd"],["A measurement is meaningful only when:",["It has a large numerical value.","It has a unit.","It has a numerical magnitude and a unit.","It has direction."],"C",3,0,"5b3b58e01611"],["In vector addition, the tail of the second vector is joined to the:",["Tail of first vector","Head of first vector","Midpoint of first vector","Origin"],"B",3,0,"07ffba4c57d3"],["The length of a vector arrow represents its:",["direction","unit","magnitude","position"],"C",3,0,"6dad38c704a4"],["Which one of the following has SI unit m²?",["area","volume","speed","density"],"A",3,0,"1f8b1a043032"],["The least count of a measuring instrument tells us:",["its length","its maximum reading","the smallest measurement it can measure","its weight"],"C",3,0,"074ebf192d75"],["Which instrument is most suitable for measuring the thickness of a sheet of paper?",["Measuring tape","Screw gauge","Vernier caliper","Stopwatch"],"B",3,0,"56ff49232b83"],["A measurement taken with a vernier caliper is 6.24 cm. If the main scale reading is 6.2 cm, the coinciding vernier division is:",["2nd","4th","24th","6th"],"B",3,0,"411540de471e"],["If the zero of the vernier scale is to the right of the zero of the main scale, the zero error is",["Positive","Negative","infinite","zero"],"A",3,0,"fc871e622035"],["Which one of the following is NOT a derived unit?",["pascal","μm (micrometer)","joule","Newton"],"B",3,0,"198c063e0fa2"],["Arrange the following SI prefixes in increasing order of magnitude: Pico, Nano, Milli, Micro",["Milli, Micro, Nano, Pico","Pico, Nano, Micro, Milli","Nano, Pico, Micro, Milli","Micro, Milli, Nano, Pico"],"B",3,0,"930bafc0e6b2"],["What is the \"head-to-tail rule\" used for?",["Subtracting vectors","Multiplying vectors","Adding vectors","Finding the magnitude of a single vector"],"C",3,0,"44d115ed2575"],["Which instrument is most suitable for measuring the diameter of a thin wire?",["Metre rule","Screw gauge","Measuring tape","Stopwatch"],"B",3,0,"56ff49